. 2001 Apr 24;98(9):5116-21", "ArticleIdList": {"ArticleId": "11309499"}}, {"Citation": "PLoS Genet. 2013;9(7):e1003598", "ArticleIdList": {"ArticleId": "23874212"}}, {"Citation": "Viruses. 2020 Sep 04;12(9):", "ArticleIdList": {"ArticleId": "32899736"}}, {"Citation": "Front Microbiol. 2017 Aug 17;8:1557", "ArticleIdList": {"ArticleId": "28861068"}}, {"Citation": "Trends Biochem Sci. 2011 Mar;36(3):159-69", "ArticleIdList": {"ArticleId": "21146412"}}, {"Citation": "Trends Cell Biol. 2016 Sep;26(9):668-679", "ArticleIdList": {"ArticleId": "27289443"}}, {"Citation": "Methods Enzymol. 2013;523:327-49", "ArticleIdList": {"ArticleId": "23422437"}}, {"Citation": "Nat Methods. 2016 Sep;13(9):731-40", "ArticleIdList": {"ArticleId": "27348712"}}, {"Citation": "Oncogene. 2001 Jun 28;20(29):3869-79", "ArticleIdList": {"ArticleId": "11439350"}}, {"Citation": "Nat Genet. 2021 Apr;53(4):435-444", "ArticleIdList": {"ArticleId": "33686287"}}, {"Citation": "Cell. 2018 May 3;173(4):958-971.e17", "ArticleIdList": {"ArticleId": "29628143"}}, {"Citation": "Nat Rev Drug Discov. 2016 Aug;15(8):533-50", "ArticleIdList": {"ArticleId": "27050677"}}, {"Citation": "Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A. 2014 Feb 18;111(7):2542-7", "ArticleIdList": {"ArticleId": "24550280"}}, {"Citation": "Nature. 2020 Jul;583(7816):459-468", "ArticleIdList": {"ArticleId": "32353859"}}, {"Citation": "Curr Opin Struct Biol. 2019 Jun;56:155-163", "ArticleIdList": {"ArticleId": "31003202"}}, {"Citation": "Cell. 2020 Apr 16;181(2):325-345.e28", "ArticleIdList": {"ArticleId": "32302571"}}, {"Citation": "PLoS Pathog. 2012;8(8):e1002845", "ArticleIdList": {"ArticleId": "22916011"}}, {"Citation": "Science. 2014 Jul 4;345(6192):98-101", "ArticleIdList": {"ArticleId": "24994655"}}, {"Citation": "Science. 2020 Dec 4;370(6521):", "ArticleIdList": {"ArticleId": "33060197"}}]}, "PublicationStatus": "epublish"}, "MedlineCitation": {"PMID": "34799561", "Article": {"Journal": {"ISSN": "2041-1723", "Title": "Nature communications", "JournalIssue": {"Issue": "1", "Volume": "12", "PubDate": {"Day": "19", "Year": "2021", "Month": "11"}, "@attributes": {"CitedMedium": "Internet"}}, "ISOAbbreviation": "Nat Commun"}, "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Viral proteins make extensive use of short peptide interaction motifs to hijack cellular host factors. However, most current large-scale methods do not identify this important class of protein-protein interactions. Uncovering peptide mediated interactions provides both a molecular understanding of viral interactions with their host and the foundation for developing novel antiviral reagents. Here we describe a viral peptide discovery approach covering 23 coronavirus strains that provides high resolution information on direct virus-host interactions. We identify 269 peptide-based interactions for 18 coronaviruses including a specific interaction between the human G3BP1/2 proteins and an ΦxFG peptide motif in the SARS-CoV-2 nucleocapsid (N) protein. This interaction supports viral replication and through its ΦxFG motif N rewires the G3BP1/2 interactome to disrupt stress granules. A peptide-based inhibitor disrupting the G3BP1/2-N interaction dampened SARS-CoV-2 infection showing that our results can be directly translated into novel specific antiviral reagents.", "CopyrightInformation": "© 2021. The Author(s)."}, "Language": "eng", "GrantList": {"Grant": [{"Agency": "Vetenskapsrådet (Swedish Research Council)", "Country": {}, "GrantID": "2020-01541"}, {"Agency": "Vetenskapsrådet (Swedish Research Council)", "Country": {}, "GrantID": "2020-04395"}, {"Agency": "Vetenskapsrådet (Swedish Research Council)", "Country": {}, "GrantID": "2017-02438"}, {"Agency": "Vetenskapsrådet (Swedish Research Council)", "Country": {}, "GrantID": "2018-05851"}, {"Agency": "Vetenskapsrådet (Swedish Research Council)", "Country": {}, "GrantID": "2020-03380"}, {"Agency": "Stiftelsen för Strategisk Forskning (Swedish Foundation for Strategic Research)", "Country": {}, "GrantID": "SB16-0039"}, {