 22;6(4):367–380. doi: 10.1016/j.chom.2009.09.005", "ArticleIdList": {"ArticleId": ["10.1016/j.chom.2009.09.005", "PMC2774833", "19837376"]}}, {"Citation": "Zan J, Liu S, Sun DN, et al. Rabies virus infection induces microtubule depolymerization to facilitate viral RNA synthesis by upregulating HDAC6. Front Cell Infect Microbiol. 2017;7:146. doi: 10.3389/fcimb.2017.00146", "ArticleIdList": {"ArticleId": ["10.3389/fcimb.2017.00146", "PMC5405082", "28491824"]}}, {"Citation": "Zandi F, Khalaj V, Goshadrou F, et al. Rabies virus matrix protein targets host actin cytoskeleton: a protein–protein interaction analysis. Pathog Dis. 2021 Jan 6;79(1). doi: 10.1093/femspd/ftaa075", "ArticleIdList": {"ArticleId": ["10.1093/femspd/ftaa075", "33289839"]}}, {"Citation": "Webb JL, Ravikumar B, Rubinsztein DC. Microtubule disruption inhibits autophagosome-lysosome fusion: implications for studying the roles of aggresomes in polyglutamine diseases. Int J Biochem Cell Biol. 2004. Dec;36(12):2541–2550. doi: 10.1016/j.biocel.2004.02.003", "ArticleIdList": {"ArticleId": ["10.1016/j.biocel.2004.02.003", "15325591"]}}, {"Citation": "Zhang Y, Jiang X, Deng Q, et al. Downregulation of MYO1C mediated by cepharanthine inhibits autophagosome-lysosome fusion through blockade of the F-actin network. J Exp Clin Cancer Res. 2019 Nov 7;38(1):457. doi: 10.1186/s13046-019-1449-8", "ArticleIdList": {"ArticleId": ["10.1186/s13046-019-1449-8", "PMC6836678", "31699152"]}}, {"Citation": "Tian D, Luo Z, Zhou M, et al. Critical role of K1685 and K1829 in the large protein of rabies virus in viral pathogenicity and immune evasion. J Virol. 2016 Jan 1;90(1):232–244. doi: 10.1128/JVI.02050-15", "ArticleIdList": {"ArticleId": ["10.1128/JVI.02050-15", "PMC4702542", "26468538"]}}, {"Citation": "Yuan Y, Fang A, Wang Z, et al. Trim25 restricts rabies virus replication by destabilizing phosphoprotein. Cell Insight. 2022. October 01;1(5):100057. doi: 10.1016/j.cellin.2022.100057", "ArticleIdList": {"ArticleId": ["10.1016/j.cellin.2022.100057", "PMC10120326", "37193556"]}}, {"Citation": "Varghese F, Bukhari AB, Malhotra R, et al. IHC Profiler: an open source plugin for the quantitative evaluation and automated scoring of immunohistochemistry images of human tissue samples. PLOS ONE. 2014;9(5):e96801. doi: 10.1371/journal.pone.0096801", "ArticleIdList": {"ArticleId": ["10.1371/journal.pone.0096801", "PMC4011881", "24802416"]}}]}, "PublicationStatus": "ppublish"}, "MedlineCitation": {"PMID": "38566321", "Article": {"Journal": {"ISSN": "1554-8635", "Title": "Autophagy", "JournalIssue": {"Issue": "8", "Volume": "20", "PubDate": {"Year": "2024", "Month": "Aug"}, "@attributes": {"CitedMedium": "Internet"}}, "ISOAbbreviation": "Autophagy"}, "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Lyssaviruses are well-known worldwide and often cause fatal encephalitis. Previous studies have shown that autophagy is beneficial for the replication of rabies virus (RABV), the representative lyssavirus, but the detailed mechanism remains obscure. In this study, we showed that the rabies virus matrix protein (RABV-M) used its PPxY motif to interact with the E3 ubiquitin-protein ligase NEDD4. NEDD4 then recruited MAP1LC3/LC3 via its LC3-interacting region (LIR). Interestingly, after binding to the ubiquitinated RABV-M, NEDD4 could bind more LC3 and enhance autophagosome accumulation, while NEDD4 knockdown significantly reduced M-induced autophagosome accumulation. Further study revealed that RABV-M prevented autophagosome-lysosome fusion and facilitated viral budding. Inhibition of RABV-M-induced autophagosome accumulation reduced the production of extracellular virus-like particles. We also found that M proteins of most lyssaviruses share the same mechanism to accumulate autophagosome by hijacking NEDD4. Collectively, this study revealed a novel strategy for lyssaviruses to achieve efficient viral replication by exploiting the host autophagy system.<b>Abbreviations:</b> ABLV: Australian bat lyssavirus; ATG5: autophagy r